1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,683
Hi, I'm Ryan Rover.

2
00:00:01,863 --> 00:00:04,293
When people imagine getting rich from a

3
00:00:04,293 --> 00:00:06,598
business, they picture tech startups,

4
00:00:06,598 --> 00:00:08,156
apps and venture capital.

5
00:00:08,336 --> 00:00:10,131
But a lot of quiet millionaires in

6
00:00:10,131 --> 00:00:12,507
America made their money doing something much

7
00:00:12,507 --> 00:00:13,247
less exciting.

8
00:00:13,427 --> 00:00:14,588
Washing cars.

9
00:00:14,768 --> 00:00:16,021
Storing boxes.

10
00:00:16,201 --> 00:00:17,142
Killing bugs.

11
00:00:17,322 --> 00:00:18,750
Pumping septic tanks.

12
00:00:18,930 --> 00:00:20,056
Boring businesses.

13
00:00:20,236 --> 00:00:22,081
And boring, it turns out,

14
00:00:22,081 --> 00:00:23,336
can be beautiful.

15
00:00:23,685 --> 00:00:25,566
Twenty five boring businesses.

16
00:00:25,746 --> 00:00:27,624
No apps, no hype,

17
00:00:27,624 --> 00:00:29,392
no viral videos.

18
00:00:29,572 --> 00:00:31,440
Just services people need,

19
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:32,589
again and again,

20
00:00:32,589 --> 00:00:35,319
whether the economy is booming or not.

21
00:00:35,668 --> 00:00:37,259
Here's why boring works.

22
00:00:37,439 --> 00:00:40,476
Boring businesses usually solve a problem people

23
00:00:40,476 --> 00:00:42,501
can't or won't solve themselves.

24
00:00:42,681 --> 00:00:44,829
They often have repeat customers.

25
00:00:45,009 --> 00:00:46,107
Many are local,

26
00:00:46,107 --> 00:00:48,741
so a giant tech company can't easily

27
00:00:48,741 --> 00:00:49,839
take them over.

28
00:00:50,019 --> 00:00:52,031
And because they're not glamorous,

29
00:00:52,031 --> 00:00:54,989
there's often less competition from people chasing

30
00:00:54,989 --> 00:00:56,114
the next big thing.

31
00:00:56,463 --> 00:00:58,349
Back in the nineteen nineties,

32
00:00:58,349 --> 00:01:00,990
Thomas Stanley and William Danko wrote The

33
00:01:00,990 --> 00:01:02,373
Millionaire Next Door.

34
00:01:02,553 --> 00:01:05,872
They found that many American millionaires were

35
00:01:05,872 --> 00:01:08,343
self employed, and many of them ran

36
00:01:08,343 --> 00:01:10,391
what the authors called dull,

37
00:01:10,391 --> 00:01:12,580
normal businesses: contractors,

38
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:14,204
pest control, cleaning,

39
00:01:14,204 --> 00:01:15,475
welding, and more.

40
00:01:15,655 --> 00:01:16,653
Not famous.

41
00:01:16,833 --> 00:01:17,669
Not flashy.

42
00:01:17,849 --> 00:01:19,753
Just profitable for a long time.

43
00:01:20,103 --> 00:01:20,999
In this video,

44
00:01:20,999 --> 00:01:23,047
twenty five of those businesses:

45
00:01:23,047 --> 00:01:24,326
how they make money,

46
00:01:24,326 --> 00:01:25,990
and what to watch out for.

47
00:01:26,170 --> 00:01:28,010
Then we'll look at the whole idea

48
00:01:28,010 --> 00:01:29,014
from three angles.

49
00:01:29,194 --> 00:01:31,296
The numbers behind small business.

50
00:01:31,476 --> 00:01:33,809
The psychology of the owners who succeed.

51
00:01:33,989 --> 00:01:35,895
And a playbook for starting or buying

52
00:01:35,895 --> 00:01:38,006
one, without betting everything you have.

53
00:01:38,357 --> 00:01:39,935
One honest warning first.

54
00:01:40,115 --> 00:01:42,823
No business is guaranteed to make money,

55
00:01:42,823 --> 00:01:44,922
and many small businesses fail.

56
00:01:45,102 --> 00:01:47,967
This video is about understanding the models,

57
00:01:47,967 --> 00:01:49,177
not about promises.

58
00:01:49,357 --> 00:01:50,019
Let's go.

59
00:01:50,369 --> 00:01:52,737
Small business counts come from the U.

60
00:01:52,917 --> 00:01:53,265
S.

61
00:01:53,445 --> 00:01:57,311
Small Business Administration's Office of Advocacy.

62
00:01:57,491 --> 00:02:00,341
Business survival rates come from the Bureau

63
00:02:00,341 --> 00:02:01,636
of Labor Statistics.

64
00:02:01,816 --> 00:02:04,559
Wage figures for skilled trades come from

65
00:02:04,559 --> 00:02:07,971
the Bureau of Labor Statistics Occupational Outlook

66
00:02:07,971 --> 00:02:08,573
Handbook.

67
00:02:08,753 --> 00:02:11,069
Where we give example numbers for a

68
00:02:11,069 --> 00:02:13,650
business, they're simple illustrations,

69
00:02:13,650 --> 00:02:15,106
not industry averages,

70
00:02:15,106 --> 00:02:18,018
because results vary enormously by location,

71
00:02:18,018 --> 00:02:19,341
management and luck.

72
00:02:19,521 --> 00:02:20,808
This is education,

73
00:02:20,808 --> 00:02:23,167
not financial or business advice.

74
00:02:23,517 --> 00:02:24,318
Angle one.

75
00:02:24,498 --> 00:02:25,264
The numbers.

76
00:02:25,444 --> 00:02:27,921
Let's look at the reality of small

77
00:02:27,921 --> 00:02:30,982
business in America before we get excited.

78
00:02:31,332 --> 00:02:33,882
The SBA Office of Advocacy counts more

79
00:02:33,882 --> 00:02:36,903
than thirty three million small businesses in

80
00:02:36,903 --> 00:02:38,112
the United States.

81
00:02:38,292 --> 00:02:40,564
They employ nearly half of all private

82
00:02:40,564 --> 00:02:41,461
sector workers.

83
00:02:41,812 --> 00:02:43,193
Thirty three million.

84
00:02:43,373 --> 00:02:44,971
That's a lot of businesses,

85
00:02:44,971 --> 00:02:47,278
and the vast majority have no employees

86
00:02:47,278 --> 00:02:47,692
at all.

87
00:02:47,872 --> 00:02:50,082
They're one person operations:

88
00:02:50,082 --> 00:02:51,924
a consultant, a handyman,

89
00:02:51,924 --> 00:02:53,619
a freelance bookkeeper.

90
00:02:53,799 --> 00:02:56,356
Most small businesses aren't trying to become

91
00:02:56,356 --> 00:02:57,549
the next big company.

92
00:02:57,729 --> 00:02:59,754
They're trying to give their owner a

93
00:02:59,754 --> 00:03:00,655
good living and,

94
00:03:00,655 --> 00:03:02,849
eventually, something valuable to sell.

95
00:03:03,199 --> 00:03:05,067
And that's the key mindset shift for

96
00:03:05,067 --> 00:03:05,950
this whole video.

97
00:03:06,130 --> 00:03:08,366
A boring business doesn't have to become

98
00:03:08,366 --> 00:03:09,764
huge to change your life.

99
00:03:09,944 --> 00:03:11,769
A single well run location,

100
00:03:11,769 --> 00:03:14,135
route or service area that pays its

101
00:03:14,135 --> 00:03:16,636
owner a solid income and builds value

102
00:03:16,636 --> 00:03:19,273
over twenty years can be the difference

103
00:03:19,273 --> 00:03:21,909
between retiring on a modest salary and

104
00:03:21,909 --> 00:03:23,667
retiring as a millionaire.

105
00:03:24,017 --> 00:03:25,619
But survival is hard.

106
00:03:25,799 --> 00:03:28,768
Bureau of Labor Statistics data shows roughly

107
00:03:28,768 --> 00:03:31,341
one in five new businesses close within

108
00:03:31,341 --> 00:03:32,463
their first year,

109
00:03:32,463 --> 00:03:34,772
and about half are gone within five

110
00:03:34,772 --> 00:03:35,168
years.

111
00:03:35,518 --> 00:03:38,112
So why talk about boring businesses at

112
00:03:38,112 --> 00:03:38,385
all?

113
00:03:38,565 --> 00:03:41,305
Because the failure rate isn't spread evenly.

114
00:03:41,485 --> 00:03:43,266
Businesses with proven demand,

115
00:03:43,266 --> 00:03:45,996
simple operations and repeat customers tend to

116
00:03:45,996 --> 00:03:48,191
have better odds than brand new ideas

117
00:03:48,191 --> 00:03:50,447
that need to convince people they want

118
00:03:50,447 --> 00:03:51,040
something.

119
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:53,477
A plumber doesn't need to convince anyone

120
00:03:53,477 --> 00:03:54,413
that pipes break.

121
00:03:54,593 --> 00:03:56,381
Demand is already there.

122
00:03:56,731 --> 00:03:58,379
And the reward can be big.

123
00:03:58,559 --> 00:04:01,464
The Federal Reserve's Survey of Consumer Finances

124
00:04:01,464 --> 00:04:04,072
has consistently found that families who own

125
00:04:04,072 --> 00:04:05,850
a business tend to have a much

126
00:04:05,850 --> 00:04:08,281
higher median net worth than families who

127
00:04:08,281 --> 00:04:08,637
don't.

128
00:04:08,817 --> 00:04:11,578
Business ownership is one of the main

129
00:04:11,578 --> 00:04:13,592
paths to wealth in America,

130
00:04:13,592 --> 00:04:17,025
alongside real estate and long term investing.

131
00:04:17,205 --> 00:04:19,275
It's riskier, but it's also one of

132
00:04:19,275 --> 00:04:21,528
the few paths where your upside isn't

133
00:04:21,528 --> 00:04:22,685
capped by a salary.

134
00:04:23,035 --> 00:04:24,973
So what makes a boring business good?

135
00:04:25,153 --> 00:04:26,581
Look for five traits.

136
00:04:26,761 --> 00:04:29,757
One, demand that doesn't depend on trends.

137
00:04:29,937 --> 00:04:31,669
People need clean clothes,

138
00:04:31,669 --> 00:04:34,068
working pipes and no termites in any

139
00:04:34,068 --> 00:04:34,534
decade.

140
00:04:34,714 --> 00:04:36,437
Two, recurring revenue:

141
00:04:36,437 --> 00:04:38,610
customers who pay every week,

142
00:04:38,610 --> 00:04:41,007
month or season instead of once.

143
00:04:41,187 --> 00:04:42,491
Three, a local moat,

144
00:04:42,491 --> 00:04:44,967
meaning the work happens in a physical

145
00:04:44,967 --> 00:04:47,053
place, so a website on the other

146
00:04:47,053 --> 00:04:49,335
side of the world can't easily take

147
00:04:49,335 --> 00:04:50,312
your customers.

148
00:04:50,662 --> 00:04:53,472
Four, a reason most people avoid it.

149
00:04:53,652 --> 00:04:55,338
Dirty, smelly, physical,

150
00:04:55,338 --> 00:04:58,852
or simply unglamorous work keeps competition lower

151
00:04:58,852 --> 00:05:01,733
than in businesses everyone dreams about.

152
00:05:01,913 --> 00:05:04,177
And five, a path to systems.

153
00:05:04,357 --> 00:05:06,954
The best boring businesses can eventually run

154
00:05:06,954 --> 00:05:08,454
with a manager and a team,

155
00:05:08,454 --> 00:05:10,532
so the owner earns from the business

156
00:05:10,532 --> 00:05:12,263
instead of being the business.

157
00:05:12,443 --> 00:05:14,017
When you look at each of the

158
00:05:14,017 --> 00:05:16,096
twenty five businesses in this video,

159
00:05:16,096 --> 00:05:18,064
check how many of these five traits

160
00:05:18,064 --> 00:05:18,457
it has.

161
00:05:18,806 --> 00:05:20,931
And here's one more number worth knowing.

162
00:05:21,111 --> 00:05:24,139
Many owners of established service businesses say

163
00:05:24,139 --> 00:05:26,672
the hardest part isn't finding customers.

164
00:05:26,852 --> 00:05:29,209
It's finding and keeping good workers.

165
00:05:29,389 --> 00:05:31,464
In the skilled trades especially,

166
00:05:31,464 --> 00:05:34,230
demand for qualified people has been strong.

167
00:05:34,410 --> 00:05:36,480
That's a challenge if you're an owner,

168
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:38,550
but it's also an opportunity if you're

169
00:05:38,550 --> 00:05:40,620
thinking about learning a trade first,

170
00:05:40,620 --> 00:05:42,581
getting paid while you learn how the

171
00:05:42,581 --> 00:05:43,780
business really works.

172
00:05:44,129 --> 00:05:44,722
Okay.

173
00:05:44,902 --> 00:05:46,782
Twenty five boring businesses.

174
00:05:46,962 --> 00:05:48,912
We'll start with the ones that run

175
00:05:48,912 --> 00:05:51,378
on machines, because machines don't call in

176
00:05:51,378 --> 00:05:51,664
sick.

177
00:05:52,014 --> 00:05:53,257
Business number one.

178
00:05:53,437 --> 00:05:54,389
Laundromats.

179
00:05:54,738 --> 00:05:57,413
Millions of Americans don't have a washer

180
00:05:57,413 --> 00:05:58,588
and dryer at home,

181
00:05:58,588 --> 00:06:00,741
especially renters in apartments.

182
00:06:00,921 --> 00:06:02,963
They need to wash clothes every week,

183
00:06:02,963 --> 00:06:04,949
no matter what the economy is doing.

184
00:06:05,129 --> 00:06:07,616
A laundromat sells machine time,

185
00:06:07,616 --> 00:06:10,647
plus extras like wash and fold service,

186
00:06:10,647 --> 00:06:13,988
vending, and sometimes pickup and delivery.

187
00:06:14,168 --> 00:06:16,368
Many owners run them with few or

188
00:06:16,368 --> 00:06:17,674
no full time staff.

189
00:06:18,024 --> 00:06:19,124
What to watch:

190
00:06:19,124 --> 00:06:20,930
machines are expensive,

191
00:06:20,930 --> 00:06:21,872
and a lease,

192
00:06:21,872 --> 00:06:25,014
water and utility costs can eat profits.

193
00:06:25,194 --> 00:06:26,867
Location is everything,

194
00:06:26,867 --> 00:06:29,559
ideally near dense apartment housing.

195
00:06:29,739 --> 00:06:32,512
Many people buy an existing laundromat rather

196
00:06:32,512 --> 00:06:33,436
than build one,

197
00:06:33,436 --> 00:06:35,284
and look closely at the age of

198
00:06:35,284 --> 00:06:37,687
the machines and the remaining years on

199
00:06:37,687 --> 00:06:39,782
the lease before signing anything.

200
00:06:40,131 --> 00:06:41,443
Business number two.

201
00:06:41,623 --> 00:06:42,599
Car washes.

202
00:06:42,948 --> 00:06:45,358
Car washes range from self serve bays

203
00:06:45,358 --> 00:06:47,116
to fully automated tunnels.

204
00:06:47,296 --> 00:06:49,301
A big trend in recent years has

205
00:06:49,301 --> 00:06:50,917
been monthly memberships:

206
00:06:50,917 --> 00:06:53,374
customers pay a flat fee for unlimited

207
00:06:53,374 --> 00:06:55,572
washes, which creates predictable,

208
00:06:55,572 --> 00:06:56,735
recurring revenue.

209
00:06:56,915 --> 00:06:59,250
Automated washes can serve a lot of

210
00:06:59,250 --> 00:07:01,385
cars per hour with a small team.

211
00:07:01,735 --> 00:07:02,684
What to watch:

212
00:07:02,684 --> 00:07:05,260
building a modern tunnel wash can cost

213
00:07:05,260 --> 00:07:08,514
millions, and competition has grown as investors

214
00:07:08,514 --> 00:07:10,547
have poured into the industry.

215
00:07:10,727 --> 00:07:14,091
Water, equipment repairs and weather all affect

216
00:07:14,091 --> 00:07:14,663
results.

217
00:07:14,843 --> 00:07:17,682
Smaller self serve washes cost less to

218
00:07:17,682 --> 00:07:19,998
buy, but usually earn less too.

219
00:07:20,178 --> 00:07:22,465
Study local competition carefully.

220
00:07:22,815 --> 00:07:24,151
Business number three.

221
00:07:24,331 --> 00:07:25,538
Self storage.

222
00:07:25,888 --> 00:07:28,169
Americans have a lot of stuff,

223
00:07:28,169 --> 00:07:29,233
and they move,

224
00:07:29,233 --> 00:07:32,274
downsize, divorce, renovate and inherit.

225
00:07:32,454 --> 00:07:34,998
Self storage rents small spaces month by

226
00:07:34,998 --> 00:07:35,380
month.

227
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:37,504
Once a facility is full,

228
00:07:37,504 --> 00:07:39,530
costs are relatively low:

229
00:07:39,530 --> 00:07:41,232
some staff, security,

230
00:07:41,232 --> 00:07:43,338
maintenance and marketing.

231
00:07:43,518 --> 00:07:45,908
Many customers stay much longer than they

232
00:07:45,908 --> 00:07:46,374
planned.

233
00:07:46,724 --> 00:07:47,744
What to watch:

234
00:07:47,744 --> 00:07:50,801
building a facility takes land and serious

235
00:07:50,801 --> 00:07:53,276
capital, and new supply in an area

236
00:07:53,276 --> 00:07:54,805
can push prices down.

237
00:07:54,985 --> 00:07:58,352
Large public companies dominate in many cities.

238
00:07:58,532 --> 00:08:01,854
Smaller investors often look at buying existing

239
00:08:01,854 --> 00:08:03,832
facilities in growing towns,

240
00:08:03,832 --> 00:08:05,811
or converting old buildings.

241
00:08:06,161 --> 00:08:07,450
Business number four.

242
00:08:07,630 --> 00:08:08,861
Vending machines.

243
00:08:09,210 --> 00:08:11,659
Vending is one of the easiest businesses

244
00:08:11,659 --> 00:08:12,577
to start small.

245
00:08:12,757 --> 00:08:13,928
You buy a machine,

246
00:08:13,928 --> 00:08:15,880
place it in a location like an

247
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:17,637
office, a gym or a factory,

248
00:08:17,637 --> 00:08:20,045
often sharing a cut with the location

249
00:08:20,045 --> 00:08:22,127
owner, and restock it regularly.

250
00:08:22,307 --> 00:08:25,098
Modern machines accept cards and phones,

251
00:08:25,098 --> 00:08:27,261
and some send sales data so you

252
00:08:27,261 --> 00:08:29,006
only restock when needed.

253
00:08:29,355 --> 00:08:30,282
What to watch:

254
00:08:30,282 --> 00:08:32,730
profits per machine are often modest,

255
00:08:32,730 --> 00:08:35,642
so the business only becomes meaningful with

256
00:08:35,642 --> 00:08:37,958
many machines and efficient routes.

257
00:08:38,138 --> 00:08:39,961
Good locations are competitive.

258
00:08:40,141 --> 00:08:42,568
Machines can be damaged or stolen.

259
00:08:42,748 --> 00:08:45,908
Treat online claims of huge passive income

260
00:08:45,908 --> 00:08:48,166
from one machine with a lot of

261
00:08:48,166 --> 00:08:48,994
skepticism.

262
00:08:49,343 --> 00:08:50,713
Business number five.

263
00:08:50,893 --> 00:08:52,368
ATM machines.

264
00:08:52,717 --> 00:08:56,167
Independent ATM owners place machines in bars,

265
00:08:56,167 --> 00:08:59,767
convenience stores, events and other spots where

266
00:08:59,767 --> 00:09:01,042
people need cash.

267
00:09:01,222 --> 00:09:03,746
Each withdrawal earns a surcharge fee,

268
00:09:03,746 --> 00:09:05,738
often split with the location.

269
00:09:05,918 --> 00:09:07,738
Once a machine is installed,

270
00:09:07,738 --> 00:09:10,014
the main jobs are keeping it filled

271
00:09:10,014 --> 00:09:11,444
with cash and running.

272
00:09:11,794 --> 00:09:12,731
What to watch:

273
00:09:12,731 --> 00:09:15,141
cash use has been declining as cards

274
00:09:15,141 --> 00:09:16,546
and phones take over,

275
00:09:16,546 --> 00:09:18,621
which is a real long term risk.

276
00:09:18,801 --> 00:09:20,963
You need cash to load the machines,

277
00:09:20,963 --> 00:09:22,261
and security matters.

278
00:09:22,441 --> 00:09:25,941
Like vending, this business usually only works

279
00:09:25,941 --> 00:09:28,681
at scale, with many machines in busy

280
00:09:28,681 --> 00:09:29,442
locations.

281
00:09:29,791 --> 00:09:32,508
Next, the trades and home services.

282
00:09:32,688 --> 00:09:35,370
These are the businesses Stanley and Danko

283
00:09:35,370 --> 00:09:37,797
kept finding among quiet millionaires.

284
00:09:38,146 --> 00:09:39,563
Business number six.

285
00:09:39,743 --> 00:09:40,149
Plumbing.

286
00:09:40,499 --> 00:09:41,764
