858
00:29:28,932 --> 00:29:31,639
and risk should never threaten your family's

859
00:29:31,639 --> 00:29:32,562
basic security.

860
00:29:32,912 --> 00:29:34,015
Step two.

861
00:29:34,195 --> 00:29:36,262
Learn the business from the inside.

862
00:29:36,442 --> 00:29:37,202
Work in it,

863
00:29:37,202 --> 00:29:38,239
even part time,

864
00:29:38,239 --> 00:29:39,484
before you own it.

865
00:29:39,664 --> 00:29:41,750
Talk to owners in other cities who

866
00:29:41,750 --> 00:29:43,530
won't see you as competition.

867
00:29:43,710 --> 00:29:45,093
Ask what surprised them,

868
00:29:45,093 --> 00:29:46,765
what their biggest costs are,

869
00:29:46,765 --> 00:29:48,551
and what they'd do differently.

870
00:29:48,731 --> 00:29:51,425
Most owners love talking about their business.

871
00:29:51,774 --> 00:29:52,726
Step three.

872
00:29:52,906 --> 00:29:55,101
Start small or buy proven.

873
00:29:55,281 --> 00:29:57,946
You can start with low cost services,

874
00:29:57,946 --> 00:29:59,531
like pressure washing,

875
00:29:59,531 --> 00:30:01,116
cleaning or lawn care,

876
00:30:01,116 --> 00:30:03,710
and test demand with almost no risk.

877
00:30:03,890 --> 00:30:06,085
Or you can buy an existing business

878
00:30:06,085 --> 00:30:08,092
with real customers and records.

879
00:30:08,272 --> 00:30:11,197
Both are usually safer than building something

880
00:30:11,197 --> 00:30:12,278
big from scratch.

881
00:30:12,627 --> 00:30:13,521
Step four.

882
00:30:13,701 --> 00:30:15,280
Do the math honestly.

883
00:30:15,460 --> 00:30:16,772
Revenue isn't profit.

884
00:30:16,952 --> 00:30:18,403
List every cost:

885
00:30:18,403 --> 00:30:20,852
equipment, insurance, fuel,

886
00:30:20,852 --> 00:30:22,847
labor, rent, licenses,

887
00:30:22,847 --> 00:30:25,114
taxes, and your own time.

888
00:30:25,294 --> 00:30:27,391
If the business only works when you

889
00:30:27,391 --> 00:30:29,429
work eighty hours a week for free,

890
00:30:29,429 --> 00:30:30,867
it's not a business yet.

891
00:30:31,047 --> 00:30:32,347
It's a hard job.

892
00:30:32,697 --> 00:30:33,638
Step five.

893
00:30:33,818 --> 00:30:35,083
Protect yourself.

894
00:30:35,263 --> 00:30:37,123
Form the right legal structure,

895
00:30:37,123 --> 00:30:38,383
get proper insurance,

896
00:30:38,383 --> 00:30:41,202
and keep business and personal money completely

897
00:30:41,202 --> 00:30:41,742
separate.

898
00:30:41,922 --> 00:30:43,341
A good accountant and,

899
00:30:43,341 --> 00:30:44,760
when buying, a lawyer,

900
00:30:44,760 --> 00:30:47,146
are worth their fees many times over.

901
00:30:47,496 --> 00:30:48,785
And step six.

902
00:30:48,965 --> 00:30:49,905
Build to sell,

903
00:30:49,905 --> 00:30:51,450
even if you never sell.

904
00:30:51,630 --> 00:30:53,099
Keep clean records,

905
00:30:53,099 --> 00:30:55,265
build systems, train people,

906
00:30:55,265 --> 00:30:57,353
and grow recurring revenue.

907
00:30:57,533 --> 00:30:59,369
Those are the things that make a

908
00:30:59,369 --> 00:31:01,032
business valuable to a buyer,

909
00:31:01,032 --> 00:31:03,096
and they're also the things that let

910
00:31:03,096 --> 00:31:05,734
you take a vacation without everything falling

911
00:31:05,734 --> 00:31:06,078
apart.

912
00:31:06,428 --> 00:31:08,871
Let me answer the questions people ask

913
00:31:08,871 --> 00:31:10,736
most about boring businesses.

914
00:31:11,085 --> 00:31:11,910
Question one.

915
00:31:12,090 --> 00:31:13,599
Which one is the best?

916
00:31:13,779 --> 00:31:15,196
There's no single best.

917
00:31:15,376 --> 00:31:17,323
The best business for you depends on

918
00:31:17,323 --> 00:31:18,622
your skills, your money,

919
00:31:18,622 --> 00:31:20,786
your location and what you can tolerate.

920
00:31:20,966 --> 00:31:23,918
Someone who loves physical work might thrive

921
00:31:23,918 --> 00:31:24,925
in landscaping.

922
00:31:25,105 --> 00:31:28,468
Someone who likes numbers might prefer bookkeeping

923
00:31:28,468 --> 00:31:29,679
or vending routes.

924
00:31:30,029 --> 00:31:30,831
Question two.

925
00:31:31,011 --> 00:31:33,066
Are these businesses really passive?

926
00:31:33,246 --> 00:31:34,105
Mostly no.

927
00:31:34,285 --> 00:31:37,570
Vending, laundromats and storage are often called

928
00:31:37,570 --> 00:31:40,252
passive, but they still need management,

929
00:31:40,252 --> 00:31:41,727
repairs and attention.

930
00:31:41,907 --> 00:31:44,762
Passive usually means you've hired someone else

931
00:31:44,762 --> 00:31:46,098
to do the active part.

932
00:31:46,278 --> 00:31:47,323
Question three.

933
00:31:47,503 --> 00:31:48,977
How much money do I need?

934
00:31:49,157 --> 00:31:51,346
Some services start with a few thousand

935
00:31:51,346 --> 00:31:52,524
dollars of equipment.

936
00:31:52,704 --> 00:31:55,487
Others, like car washes or storage,

937
00:31:55,487 --> 00:31:56,919
can cost millions.

938
00:31:57,268 --> 00:31:58,255
Question four.

939
00:31:58,435 --> 00:32:00,107
Should I buy a franchise?

940
00:32:00,287 --> 00:32:03,428
Franchises offer a proven system and brand,

941
00:32:03,428 --> 00:32:05,546
but come with fees and rules.

942
00:32:05,726 --> 00:32:08,914
Read the franchise disclosure document carefully,

943
00:32:08,914 --> 00:32:11,517
and talk to current and former franchise

944
00:32:11,517 --> 00:32:12,948
owners before signing.

945
00:32:13,128 --> 00:32:14,103
Question five.

946
00:32:14,283 --> 00:32:16,477
Will AI replace these businesses?

947
00:32:16,657 --> 00:32:19,085
Many of them involve physical work in

948
00:32:19,085 --> 00:32:21,709
specific places, which is much harder to

949
00:32:21,709 --> 00:32:23,414
automate than office work.

950
00:32:23,594 --> 00:32:24,860
That's part of their appeal.

951
00:32:25,209 --> 00:32:26,336
Question six.

952
00:32:26,516 --> 00:32:27,967
Can I run one of these while

953
00:32:27,967 --> 00:32:28,745
keeping my job?

954
00:32:28,925 --> 00:32:29,877
Some, yes.

955
00:32:30,057 --> 00:32:32,909
Vending routes, small cleaning contracts,

956
00:32:32,909 --> 00:32:34,927
pressure washing on weekends,

957
00:32:34,927 --> 00:32:37,362
or a laundromat with a good manager

958
00:32:37,362 --> 00:32:39,519
can be started alongside a job.

959
00:32:39,699 --> 00:32:41,755
It's often the smartest way to test

960
00:32:41,755 --> 00:32:44,281
a business, because your salary covers your

961
00:32:44,281 --> 00:32:46,514
life while the business proves itself.

962
00:32:46,694 --> 00:32:48,909
Just be honest about your time and

963
00:32:48,909 --> 00:32:51,906
energy, and check your employment contract for

964
00:32:51,906 --> 00:32:52,557
conflicts.

965
00:32:52,906 --> 00:32:53,882
Question seven.

966
00:32:54,062 --> 00:32:56,102
Should I use my retirement savings to

967
00:32:56,102 --> 00:32:56,929
buy a business?

968
00:32:57,109 --> 00:32:58,294
Be very careful.

969
00:32:58,474 --> 00:33:00,968
There are complex arrangements that allow it,

970
00:33:00,968 --> 00:33:02,964
but they carry real risks and rules,

971
00:33:02,964 --> 00:33:04,904
and if the business fails you could

972
00:33:04,904 --> 00:33:07,344
lose both your business and your retirement.

973
00:33:07,524 --> 00:33:10,132
Most people are better off using savings

974
00:33:10,132 --> 00:33:11,958
outside retirement accounts,

975
00:33:11,958 --> 00:33:13,393
a small business loan,

976
00:33:13,393 --> 00:33:14,697
or seller financing,

977
00:33:14,697 --> 00:33:16,914
where the seller lets you pay part

978
00:33:16,914 --> 00:33:18,414
of the price over time.

979
00:33:18,763 --> 00:33:19,530
Let's recap.

980
00:33:19,710 --> 00:33:21,901
The machine businesses:

981
00:33:21,901 --> 00:33:24,188
laundromats, car washes,

982
00:33:24,188 --> 00:33:27,999
self storage, vending machines and ATMs.

983
00:33:28,179 --> 00:33:30,141
The trades: plumbing,

984
00:33:30,141 --> 00:33:34,530
HVAC, electrical, pest control and landscaping.

985
00:33:34,710 --> 00:33:36,425
The jobs nobody wants:

986
00:33:36,425 --> 00:33:38,062
septic, junk removal,

987
00:33:38,062 --> 00:33:42,349
commercial cleaning, pressure washing and pool service.

988
00:33:42,700 --> 00:33:44,047
Then auto repair,

989
00:33:44,047 --> 00:33:45,949
towing, dumpster rental,

990
00:33:45,949 --> 00:33:47,931
bookkeeping and tax prep,

991
00:33:47,931 --> 00:33:49,596
and funeral services.

992
00:33:49,776 --> 00:33:52,225
And the land and local businesses:

993
00:33:52,225 --> 00:33:54,026
mobile home and RV parks,

994
00:33:54,026 --> 00:33:56,979
parking lots, window and gutter cleaning,

995
00:33:56,979 --> 00:33:59,644
tire shops, and sign and print shops.

996
00:33:59,995 --> 00:34:01,318
And the three angles.

997
00:34:01,498 --> 00:34:03,883
The numbers: tens of millions of small

998
00:34:03,883 --> 00:34:06,518
businesses, about half survive five years,

999
00:34:06,518 --> 00:34:08,652
but owners tend to build much more

1000
00:34:08,652 --> 00:34:09,091
wealth.

1001
00:34:09,271 --> 00:34:11,866
The psychology: results over image,

1002
00:34:11,866 --> 00:34:15,647
systems, patience, careful money and obsession with

1003
00:34:15,647 --> 00:34:16,388
customers.

1004
00:34:16,568 --> 00:34:17,870
And the playbook:

1005
00:34:17,870 --> 00:34:19,479
keep your foundation,

1006
00:34:19,479 --> 00:34:21,164
learn from the inside,

1007
00:34:21,164 --> 00:34:23,156
start small or buy proven,

1008
00:34:23,156 --> 00:34:24,305
do honest math,

1009
00:34:24,305 --> 00:34:27,063
protect yourself, and build to sell.

1010
00:34:27,414 --> 00:34:29,670
And here's the bigger lesson behind all

1011
00:34:29,670 --> 00:34:31,001
twenty five businesses.

1012
00:34:31,181 --> 00:34:33,563
Wealth often hides in plain sight,

1013
00:34:33,563 --> 00:34:36,435
in the services everybody uses and nobody

1014
00:34:36,435 --> 00:34:37,346
thinks about.

1015
00:34:37,526 --> 00:34:39,291
The laundromat on the corner.

1016
00:34:39,471 --> 00:34:41,622
The pest control truck in your neighbor's

1017
00:34:41,622 --> 00:34:42,094
driveway.

1018
00:34:42,274 --> 00:34:44,807
The company that pumps the septic tank

1019
00:34:44,807 --> 00:34:46,141
at the edge of town.

1020
00:34:46,321 --> 00:34:48,338
Behind many of them is an owner

1021
00:34:48,338 --> 00:34:49,444
who saw a boring,

1022
00:34:49,444 --> 00:34:51,918
steady need, served it well for years,

1023
00:34:51,918 --> 00:34:54,651
and quietly built something worth far more

1024
00:34:54,651 --> 00:34:55,562
than a salary.

1025
00:34:55,742 --> 00:34:57,844
You don't need a brilliant idea.

1026
00:34:58,024 --> 00:34:59,273
You need a real need,

1027
00:34:59,273 --> 00:35:00,343
a lot of patience,

1028
00:35:00,343 --> 00:35:02,366
and the discipline to run it well.

1029
00:35:02,716 --> 00:35:04,647
And if owning a business isn't for

1030
00:35:04,647 --> 00:35:06,466
you, that's completely fine too.

1031
00:35:06,646 --> 00:35:08,759
You can still benefit from the same

1032
00:35:08,759 --> 00:35:09,060
idea.

1033
00:35:09,240 --> 00:35:11,377
Broad index funds make you a part

1034
00:35:11,377 --> 00:35:13,513
owner of thousands of businesses,

1035
00:35:13,513 --> 00:35:15,196
boring and exciting alike.

1036
00:35:15,376 --> 00:35:17,612
Owning, in one form or another,

1037
00:35:17,612 --> 00:35:19,777
is how most wealth gets built.

1038
00:35:19,957 --> 00:35:22,037
The question is just which form fits

1039
00:35:22,037 --> 00:35:22,615
your life.

1040
00:35:22,966 --> 00:35:24,463
So here's your homework.

1041
00:35:24,643 --> 00:35:26,837
Pick two businesses from this list that

1042
00:35:26,837 --> 00:35:28,637
fit your skills and your budget.

1043
00:35:28,817 --> 00:35:30,843
This week, call one owner and ask

1044
00:35:30,843 --> 00:35:32,439
them about their business.

1045
00:35:32,619 --> 00:35:34,965
That one conversation will teach you more

1046
00:35:34,965 --> 00:35:36,223
than a hundred videos,

1047
00:35:36,223 --> 00:35:37,310
including this one.

1048
00:35:37,490 --> 00:35:39,146
Ask what they love about it,

1049
00:35:39,146 --> 00:35:40,566
what they hate about it,

1050
00:35:40,566 --> 00:35:42,578
and what they wish they'd known on

1051
00:35:42,578 --> 00:35:43,051
day one.

1052
00:35:43,231 --> 00:35:44,888
If you want the full plan for

1053
00:35:44,888 --> 00:35:47,003
building wealth, it's in my playbook,

1054
00:35:47,003 --> 00:35:48,374
link in the description.

1055
00:35:48,554 --> 00:35:49,657
I'm Ryan Rover.

1056
00:35:49,837 --> 00:35:50,987
See you in the next one.
